     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>     Just being practical, you might replace your actual covariate with another variable which is equal to the real covariate in most groups but is just random noise in the one group. If you leave the covariate&#39;s paths fixed at 0 in that one group where your real covariate has no variance, that should address your problem. You could make these random numbers ordinal by using the cut() standard function in R.</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Tue, Nov 21, 2023 at 11:07 AM Alexander Jung &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jungalexa...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI Adjusted&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Liberation Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both;color:rgb(12,13,14)\">Dear Group,</p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI Adjusted&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Liberation Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both;color:rgb(12,13,14)\">I try to fit a multigroup SEM in lavaan.</p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI Adjusted&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Liberation Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both;color:rgb(12,13,14)\">In one of my groups (group 1) all values for a specific covariate are the same (i.e., all students in this group are in grade 5), in my other two groups however this covariate (grade) varies between students. I want to compare other regression coefficients between groups, while controling for the grade in all groups but in group 1. (In other groups 2 and 3 I scale the covariate &quot;grade&quot; as a deviation of grade 5, the level of all students in group 1). </p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI Adjusted&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Liberation Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both;color:rgb(12,13,14)\">This seems to not be easily possible, lavaan gives the following error message: &quot;lavaan ERROR: some variables have no variance in group 1: grade&quot;.</p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI Adjusted&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Liberation Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both;color:rgb(12,13,14)\">This is my (simplified) model syntax:</p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI Adjusted&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Liberation Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both;color:rgb(12,13,14)\">    T2   ~ T1 + S1 + grade<br>    S2   ~ S1 + T1 + grade<br></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI Adjusted&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Liberation Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both;color:rgb(12,13,14)\">    T1   ~~ S1 + grade<br>    S1   ~~ grade <br></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI Adjusted&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Liberation Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both;color:rgb(12,13,14)\">Can someone give me advice on how to implement my intended analysis?</p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI Adjusted&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Liberation Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both;color:rgb(12,13,14)\">(I would need an approach that also works for categorical covariates, as the same is also the case for a categorical second covariate &quot;school-type&quot; that varies in groups 2 and 3 but not in group 1)<br></p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI Adjusted&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Liberation Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both;color:rgb(12,13,14)\">I would be super happy about advice.</p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI Adjusted&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Liberation Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both;color:rgb(12,13,14)\">All the Best,</p><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.1em;padding:0px;border:0px;font-variant-numeric:inherit;font-variant-east-asian:inherit;font-variant-alternates:inherit;font-stretch:inherit;line-height:inherit;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI Adjusted&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Liberation Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-kerning:inherit;font-feature-settings:inherit;font-size:15px;vertical-align:baseline;box-sizing:inherit;clear:both;color:rgb(12,13,14)\">Alex</p>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;lavaan&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked r